@*
    OdsRecordBody — the expanded-record body (Odyssey Design System · components/RecordBody).

    Extracted from OdsRecordCard so a TABLE-based record list renders the identical detail
    surface: a record card's expanded body and an OdsRecordTable's expanded detail row are the
    same thing and must look the same. One padded column of slots in a fixed order —
    Alert → Details → Content → Sections — which a caller cannot reorder, which is the point.

    OdsRecordCard composes this for its own body. A table detail panel renders it directly with
    InTable: the card's hairline top divider gives way to the table's primary accent rule, and the
    panel sits on the surface colour against the detail cell's background tint. OdsRecordTable's
    own panel steps aside for it (padding and rule), so the body is the one surface.

    Accent / AccentSoft set --rec / --rec-soft, which the OdsInfoTileGrid inside Details reads for
    its tile icon chips. Inside an OdsRecordCard they are already set on the card, so pass them only
    when rendering standalone. Styled by the global .odc-record-body block in
    wwwroot/css/odyssey-components.css.
*@

<div id="@Id" class="@BodyClass" style="@BodyStyle">
    @Alert
    @Details
    @Content
    @Sections
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Slot 1 — an OdsProblemAlert / OdsAlert. Renders first, above everything else.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Alert { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Slot 2 — the record's field set, an <see cref="OdsInfoTileGrid"/> of
    /// <see cref="OdsInfoTile"/>s.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Details { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Slot 3 — prose / chart / summary content below the field set.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Content { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Slot 4 — the sub-collections, each introduced by an <see cref="OdsSectionDivider"/>.
    /// (The DS calls this slot <c>children</c>; it is named here, as on OdsRecordCard, so content
    /// cannot land in the wrong slot by accident.)</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Sections { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Record accent (sets <c>--rec</c>) — only when rendering outside an OdsRecordCard.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Accent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Soft form of the accent (sets <c>--rec-soft</c>).</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? AccentSoft { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Rendering inside an OdsRecordTable detail cell rather than an OdsRecordCard.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool InTable { get; set; }

    /// <summary>DOM id — the target of the owning trigger's aria-controls.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Id { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Extra CSS class(es) appended to the root.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Style { get; set; }

    private string BodyClass =>
        string.Join(' ', new[] { "odc-record-body", InTable ? "in-table" : null, Class }
            .Where(c => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(c)));

    private string? BodyStyle
    {
        get
        {
            var rec = string.IsNullOrEmpty(Accent) ? null : $"--rec:{Accent};";
            var soft = string.IsNullOrEmpty(AccentSoft) ? null : $"--rec-soft:{AccentSoft};";
            var style = $"{rec}{soft}{Style}";
            return style.Length == 0 ? null : style;
        }
    }
}
